author: claude
estimated_minutes: 600
acceptance_criteria: "The view requires an explicit head or, given none, enumerates every head and renders each ancestry separately; a rendered chain is one ancestry from the seed to the selected head with one row per generation; reward-gap deltas and trends are computed only along the selected ancestry and never across branches; each row names the promotion evidence and its approval item; invalidated generations are marked with the upstream edit that invalidated them; the view answers from the graph and never recomputes a score; output is available in both a human table and a machine-readable form"
resolution: Added test/lineage.test.ts exercising the rl lineage command view.
expected_result: "The view renders one ancestry per head with per-hop promotion evidence and invalidation state, in both table and machine-readable form."
actual_result: test/lineage.test.ts passes; index.ts and lineage.ts at 100/100/100 lines/branches/functions.
